{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR6, named declaration seals. Head 7f9acdc5829c1f67710b0e9e4f6f9612e0d0ba7a, branch request/br6-declaration-seals-20261027. Main bb23e50f is the merge base. The delta is 4 paths, 1,211 insertions and 18 deletions: scripts/security-entry-points.mjs (88 lines appended), scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs, the note and the manifest. Review request 80dccb1e, checker promise 7f98687a, request aac55021, builder promise 9b0a4edc, standing release 5e61fd63, and my agreement report 15b1ed7e (ratified a00ae388). Primary artifact 642aa199 (the PD-2 note), first of 6. gs inspect shows it resting on promise 9b0a4edc, request aac55021, release 5e61fd63 and agreement 15b1ed7e.\n\nRead order: the note in full; agreement 15b1ed7e; namedSourceSeals in full; the test diff (the table, assertOwner and the four new cases); the raw control records; the gate record; the manifest and the sealed directory. I did not run any suite again.\n\nAgainst agreement 15b1ed7e:\n1. Five owners converted, 150 declarations plus five module records. The table holds 155 named lines: object 1, worker 28, commands 74 (entryLine included), service 30, core 17. Each is keyed file:declaration on its own line, $module first and then declarations in source order. The seven whole-file entries for these files are removed (object.ts appeared twice). Both object categories now point at namedOwners[\"packages/scope/src/object.ts\"].\n2. The selector uses the same parse and the same metadata cleaning as sourceSeal. Functions and classes are sealed as their original AST, whole classes included. A variable record keeps its declaration kind and declarator, and its initializer also stays in the module record.\n3. The module record keeps, in order:\n   - value imports, with type-only specifiers dropped and side-effect imports kept;\n   - exports, re-exports and export *;\n   - anonymous default exports, in full;\n   - every top-level executable statement;\n   - the declaration inventory of name, kind and export form.\n   Function and class bodies are nulled there, so a body is not counted twice.\n4. Fail closed: invalid or duplicate selectors, a reserved name, destructuring, a duplicate runtime declaration, unsupported syntax, a top-level statement of an unknown kind, a missing selected declaration and an unselected runtime declaration all refuse. TypeScript enums, namespaces and overload signatures are not in the accepted lists, so one appearing in these five files refuses until the selector is reviewed. That is the right direction.\n5. No exemption: entryLine is selected, and the first control shows its edit changes its own record only.\n6. Unchanged: declaration(), load(), servedInventory(), assertInventory(), sourceSeal() and the route document. The new code is appended after sourceSeal, and the note's probe found all 68 unconverted owners equal, the three BR8 owners included.\n7. A failure message is one line, \"\u003cfile:declaration\u003e actual \u003chash\u003e; Review source before adopting a new seal.\", and never prints source.\n\nControls (raw output read). Each has one healthy baseline pass and one mutant failure at its named case:\n- declaration content: a real routedRequest edit, the body helper and entryLine each change only their own record;\n- module content: an import source rewrite, an import binding rename, an added side-effect import and an added statement each change the module record;\n- runtime completeness: missing, duplicate, new and unsupported declarations refuse.\nThe owning file's fourth new case covers a class constructor, a field and a private method through both object categories. The note records eight passing cases in the owning file.\n\nValidation:\n- The ordinary gate at 2ba8595f (tree 3c12c0e7) passed.\n- After the gate only the note and the manifest change, so the documents-only rule applies.\n- The manifest verifies against the sealed directory: 139 files, 0 bad, nothing writable, SHA256SUMS all OK.\n- check-notes bb23e50f..7f9acdc5 reports 0 warnings, and git diff --check is clean.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One selector function beside sourceSeal, with complete coverage enforced by the inventory rather than by a list someone must remember to extend. Two heads that edit different declarations now touch different lines of the table.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Coverage is not narrower than before: every runtime declaration and all module-level execution in the five files are sealed, and the declaration inventory catches additions. The tripwire still says nothing about imported implementations, as before; their own seals and runtime witnesses are unchanged.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. Nit: the removed whole-file entries carried one-line rationale comments (for example \"R11 host admission wiring\"). The named table has none. A short comment on each owner block, saying why the file is security-relevant, would keep that context for the next reviewer.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 7f9acdc5. The builder lands. The landing closes BR6 request aac55021. No builder deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:642aa199f49166e1fe5b88f3be5cec1dc1465c7a","binding":"assigned","head":"7f9acdc5829c1f67710b0e9e4f6f9612e0d0ba7a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f98687a16ff94b783cc26b80bd0862d7018c718\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9b0a4edc877eda9b00b209caf14f6ada05046d05\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f98687a16ff94b783cc26b80bd0862d7018c718","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}